Feature: Masking Invoice Numbers in d_product_revenue_clone Table
  Ensure that the last four digits of invoice_number in the d_product_revenue_clone table are masked with '*' to protect customer information.

  Background:
    Given the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" does not exist
    When I drop the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" if it exists
    And I create a replica of "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue" as "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"

  Scenario: Successfully mask the last four digits of a valid invoice_number
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table exists
    And the "invoice_number" column contains valid bigint values
    When I apply the PySpark masking logic to the "invoice_number" column
    Then the last four digits of each "invoice_number" should be replaced with "****"
    And the "invoice_number" column should be of type string

  Scenario Outline: Masking various invoice_number formats
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table exists
    When I mask the "invoice_number" value "<invoice_number>"
    Then the masked "invoice_number" should be "<masked_invoice_number>"

    Examples:
      | invoice_number | masked_invoice_number |
      | 1234234534     | 123423****            |
      | 9876543210     | 987654****            |
      | 5678901234     | 567890****            |
      | 1020304050     | 102030****            |

  Scenario: Handle invoice_number with fewer than four digits
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table exists
    And the "invoice_number" value is "123"
    When I apply the PySpark masking logic to the "invoice_number" column
    Then an error "Invoice number must have at least four digits to mask." should be raised

  Scenario: Source table does not exist during cloning
    Given the table "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue" does not exist
    When I attempt to create a replica of "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue" as "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone"
    Then an error "Source table purgo_playground.d_product_revenue does not exist." should be returned

  Scenario: Data type conversion for masked invoice_number
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table exists
    When I change the data type of "invoice_number" from bigint to string
    Then the data type of "invoice_number" should be string
    And existing numeric operations on "invoice_number" should be disabled

  Scenario: Ensure data integrity after masking
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table exists with foreign key relationships
    When I apply the PySpark masking logic to the "invoice_number" column
    Then all foreign key constraints should remain intact
    And related tables should reflect the masked "invoice_number" appropriately

  Scenario: Automated masking process execution
    Given the masking process is scheduled to run daily
    When the daily schedule triggers the masking job
    Then the "invoice_number" column in "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" should have the last four digits masked with "*"
    And a success message "Masking process completed successfully." should be logged

  Scenario: Validate masked invoice_number format
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table exists
    When I retrieve the "invoice_number" from the table
    Then each "invoice_number" should match the regex "^\d{6}\*{4}$"

  Scenario: Error handling for unexpected data types in invoice_number
    Given the "purgo_playground.d_product_revenue_clone" table exists
    And the "invoice_number" column contains non-bigint values
    When I apply the PySpark masking logic to the "invoice_number" column
    Then an error "Invalid data type for invoice_number. Expected bigint." should be raised
